# Code Quality & Verification Rules

- **Verify before declaring success**: Run builds and tests to verify changes before marking tasks done.
- **Inspect logs before diagnosing errors**: Base diagnoses strictly on empirical log evidence.
- **No superficial symptom patches**: Fix root causes instead of swallowing exceptions, returning dummy fallbacks, or deleting tests.
- **Preserve semantic line breaks**: Follow semantic line breaks (SemBr) in Markdown prose documents.
- **Use GitHub markdown links**: Use `[filename](file:///path/to/file)` format for file paths and line ranges.
